{"id": "21", "question": "magellan of virginia provider", "gt": "Magellan of Virginia is the Behavioral Health Services Administrator for the Virginia Department of Medical Assistance Services. They administer behavioral health services for members enrolled in Virginia’s Medicaid and FAMIS programs. The site is also for providers, offering them resources like weekly Q&A sessions each Friday from 1 p.m. - 2:30 p.m. where they can address their questions and issues. Additionally, they offer continuing education clock hours/credits for e-learning courses, approved by organizations like the American Psychological Association and the Association of Social Work Boards.", "pred": "Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider that administers services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members in Virginia, hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., and ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Magellan of Virginia is a behavioral health services provider that administers services for Medicaid and FAMIS program members in Virginia, hosts weekly provider Q&A sessions every Friday from 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m., and ensures quality behavioral health services for Virginia Medicaid enrollees through partnerships with members, providers, and stakeholders.", "time_sec": 6.523, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.1, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
