{"id": "53", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the benefits of using a water pick (also known as a Waterpik) include:\n\n1. Helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by eliminating germs and plaque.\n2. Being a great oral care tool for removing food from areas that brushing cannot access.\n3. Massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth to reduce the risk of gingivitis.\n4. Being an alternative to flossing and potentially offering similar benefits.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide information on other potential benefits of using a water pick, such as its ability to reach areas between teeth or its effectiveness in reducing plaque buildup.", "pred": "Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and clean better around teeth and gums by removing food from inaccessible areas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and clean better around teeth and gums by removing food from inaccessible areas.", "time_sec": 5.835, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 33.9, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "54", "question": "benefits of a water pick", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the benefits of a water pick include:\n\n* Helping to keep teeth, gums, mouth, and overall body healthier by eliminating pesky germs and plaque that are difficult to remove with a toothbrush.\n* Massaging and stimulating soft tissue in the mouth to reduce the risk of gingivitis.\n* Cleaning better around the teeth and gums, removing food particles from areas that brushing cannot access.\n\nTherefore, using a water pick can be an effective addition to your oral hygiene routine, complementing traditional brushing and flossing methods.", "pred": "Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and clean better around teeth and gums by removing food from inaccessible areas.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Water picks help maintain oral health by shooting a strong stream of water at the gum line to eliminate germs and plaque, especially in areas brushing cannot reach. They massage and stimulate soft tissue, reducing the risk of gingivitis, and clean better around teeth and gums by removing food from inaccessible areas.", "time_sec": 5.758, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 38.78, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "55", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "You can prevent birds from building nests on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch and the top of the porch if it has open rafters. This will block the birds from reaching spaces they often choose to build their nests. If you have a light fixture, you can also install bird netting over it, but make sure the netting is nonflammable and safe to use around light bulbs and doesn't entangle birds. Another method is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch, as this can scare birds away. Remember to move the plastic hawk periodically to prevent the birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "time_sec": 12.231, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 57.85, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "57", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "To prevent birds from building a nest on your porch, you can attach bird netting to the eves and top of your porch with staples. Additionally, you can install bird netting over your light fixture to deter birds from accessing it. Another option is to mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away. It's important to note that any product used to deter birds should be nonflammable and safe to use.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "time_sec": 7.184, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 53.61, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "58", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch using a staple gun. This will prevent birds from reaching those spaces they often choose to build their nests, which can block your ventilation systems, are made from flammable materials, and bird droppings can transmit disease. (Passage 1:4)\n2. Install bird netting over the top of your light fixture to block the birds' access to it. Choose a netting that is non-flammable and safe to use around light bulbs, and make sure it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds. (Passage 2:1)\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch. The sight of a predator can scare the birds away from the area and keep them from inhabiting your porch. Move the plastic hawk periodically to keep the birds from becoming accustomed to its presence. (Passage 3:1)\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, you can keep birds from building nests on your porch by using bird netting, installing bird netting over your light fixture, or mounting a plastic hawk near your porch.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "time_sec": 7.406, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 35.48, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "59", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "time_sec": 7.286, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.22, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "60", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building a nest on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds away.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to keep birds from building a nest on your porch is:\n\nAttach bird netting to the eaves or install bird netting over the light fixture, and/or mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch.", "pred": "You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: You can keep birds from building a nest on your porch by attaching bird netting to the eves around the perimeter of your porch or to the top of the porch if it has open rafters, using a nonflammable and safe netting to cover light fixtures, and mounting a plastic hawk on or near your porch while moving it periodically to prevent birds from becoming accustomed to it.", "time_sec": 7.101, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 41.74, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
