{"id": "63", "question": "set default browser to windows", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here are the steps to set the default browser to Windows:\n\nMethod 1:\n\n1. Open the Settings app by clicking the Start menu and then clicking the Settings icon, or by using the Windows + I keyboard shortcut.\n2. In the Settings app, click the first option titled System (display, notifications, apps, power).\n3. In the left-pane, click Default apps.\n4. On the right-side, scroll down the page to see Web browser section.\n5. Click on the Edge browser entry (or any browser other than Chrome) to reveal Choose an app, and then click Google Chrome to set it as default browser.\n\nAlternatively, you can also set Mozilla Firefox as your default Windows browser by following these steps:\n\n1. Open your Firefox browser.\n2. Click on the Firefox menu button, represented by three horizontal lines and located in the upper right-hand corner of the browser window.\n3. When the pop-out menu appears, select Options.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.864, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 4.58, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
