d small intestines (too fast, slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include violent episodes of diarrhea, constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps in the lower half of the belly that worsen after meals and improve after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating.", "time_sec": 14.11, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.68, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "84", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here are the symptoms and causes of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) based on the given passages:\n\nSymptoms:\n\n* Diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea)\n* Constipation\n* Constipation alternating with diarrhea\n* Belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement\n* A lot of gas or bloating\n\nCauses:\n\n* Abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements\n* Increased awareness of bodily functions\n* Disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract\n* Alterations in the GI tract motility\n* Abnormal nervous system signals\n* Increased sensitivity to pain\n* Food intolerances\n* Poor absorption of sugars or acids in food\n\nIt's worth noting that the exact cause of IBS is still unknown, and it's believed to be a complex interaction of various factors.", "pred": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is currently unknown, but it is thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. IBS-D is a type of IBS characterized by diarrhea. Risk factors for IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast, slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include violent episodes of diarrhea, constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps in the lower half of the belly that worsen after meals and improve after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is currently unknown, but it is thought to result from a combination of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, and a disruption in the communication between the brain and the GI tract. IBS-D is a type of IBS characterized by diarrhea. Risk factors for IBS include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (too fast, slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include violent episodes of diarrhea, constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps in the lower half of the belly that worsen after meals and improve after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating.", "time_sec": 13.961, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.77, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "85", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end. Then, take another clean slide and holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry and label clearly. Once dried, place them in the provided slide transport containers. Always avoid coming into contact with another person's blood and if it is unavoidable, wear rubber gloves.", "pred": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, hold it at a 45-degree angle, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided slide transport containers. Always avoid contact with another person's blood and wear rubber gloves if unavoidable, as blood can carry diseases that can be transferred from person to person.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, hold it at a 45-degree angle, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided slide transport containers. Always avoid contact with another person's blood and wear rubber gloves if unavoidable, as blood can carry diseases that can be transferred from person to person.", "time_sec": 12.281, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 87.8, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
