{"id": "88", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here are the steps to prepare a blood slide based on the provided passages:\n\n1. First, sterilize a needle with a flame as described in Passage 1.\n2. Next, obtain a blood sample by pricking your finger or using a blood donation kit. This will require adult supervision, especially if you are doing it yourself.\n3. Place a drop of blood towards one end of a clean glass slide as instructed in Passage 2.\n4. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide through capillary action. Gently push the blood along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Repeat this step to make two smears.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely before labeling them clearly and placing them in the provided slide transport containers as suggested in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a flat surface and add one small drop of blood to one end. Take another clean slide, hold it at a 45-degree angle, and touch the blood with one end of the slide so the blood runs along the edge of the slide by capillary action. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label clearly. Once dried, place the slides in provided slide transport containers. Always avoid contact with another person's blood and wear rubber gloves if unavoidable, as blood can carry diseases that can be transferred from person to person.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To prepare a blood slide, first sterilize a needle with a flame. Place a clean glass slide on a