{"id": "124", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4\" and set and level them according to the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the plans. Check for squareness and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Cut two more 4 x 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids and, when the frame is square, toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The size of the shed can be adjusted as needed.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.767, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
