{"id": "183", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 1.837, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 0, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "185", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "To make chicken tender in a crock pot, you can cook it on low for 6 - 8 hours or until done. Alternatively, you can cook it on high for 1 hour, then on low for about 5 hours or until done. Another option is cooking it for 4 hours on high.", "pred": "It takes 6 - 8 hours on low or 1 hour on high then 5 hours on low to make chicken tender in a crock pot.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: It takes 6 - 8 hours on low or 1 hour on high then 5 hours on low to make chicken tender in a crock pot.", "time_sec": 3.709, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.5, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "189", "question": "how long does it take to make chicken tender in crock pot", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the answer to the question \"How long does it take to make chicken tender in a crock pot?\" is:\n\n6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.\n\nThe first passage suggests cooking the chicken on low for 6-8 hours, or 1 hour on high and then 5 hours on low. The second passage repeats the same information. The third passage provides additional information that chicken breast will always come out tender as long as there is enough moisture, and suggests cooking it for 4 hours on high if you're short on time.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question is 6-8 hours on low heat, or 4 hours on high heat if you're short on time.", "pred": "It takes 6 - 8 hours on low or 1 hour on high then 5 hours on low to make chicken tender in a crock pot.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: It takes 6 - 8 hours on low or 1 hour on high then 5 hours on low to make chicken tender in a crock pot.", "time_sec": 3.684, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 26.8, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "191", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "To attach multiple picture frames together, you can use small hinges to connect the frames. Lay the frames beside each other to determine the desired arrangement. For two frames, use identical ones, and for three frames, either choose three identical frames or use a larger one as the middle frame. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges. Attach the hinges to securely join the frames.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "time_sec": 8.007, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 74.55, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "193", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps for attaching multiple picture frames together:\n\nPassage 1: Table-Stand Grouping\nTo join two or three frames together, you can use identical frames or one larger frame as the middle piece. Place the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect, and then mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nPassage 2: Hanging Multiple Pictures Together\nBefore attaching the frames together, test different arrangements of the group of multiple pictures on the floor. Once you have decided on the layout, screw the frames to the backer board, repeating the process for each frame. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them on the wall to enjoy the finished result.\n\nPassage 3: Attaching Frames Together\nTo attach two frames together, place them back to back and mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. The placement should be the same distance from the bottom edge of each frame to ensure stability when the grouped pictures are placed on a table. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nIn conclusion, the recommended method for attaching multiple picture frames together involves using identical or matching frames, marking the hinge placement on the connecting sides, and attaching small hinges to join the frames together. It's also important to test different arrangements of the group of pictures on the floor before attaching the frames together, and to ensure that the frames are securely attached to the backer board before hanging them on the wall.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "time_sec": 8.052, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.34, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "194", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to attach multiple picture frames together:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding (Passage 1).\n2. Lay the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect (Passage 1).\n3. Mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides of the frames, making sure the placement is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame (Passage 1).\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames (Passage 1).\n5. Test ideas by laying the group of multiple pictures out on the floor first (Passage 2).\n6. Screw the frame to the backer board, repeat with each frame, and attach a hanging wire to the back (Passage 3).\n\nIt's important to note that the passages do not provide specific information on how to attach multiple frames together other than the steps mentioned above. Therefore, if more detailed instructions are needed, it may be best to consult additional resources or seek advice from a professional framer.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "time_sec": 7.805, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 39.55, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "195", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo attach multiple picture frames together, you can follow these steps:\n\n1. Select two or three frames of the same wood molding.\n2. Lay them beside each other to see if you like the effect.\n3. Put two frames together back to back, and mark the hinge placement. The placement must be the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame to ensure that the grouped pictures stand securely on the table top.\n4. Attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.\n5. Repeat the process for additional frames, ensuring that the hinge placement is consistent across all frames.\n6. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the grouped frames and hang them up.\n\nTherefore, the answer is: Select frames with the same wood molding, lay them together, mark hinge placement, attach hinges, and attach a hanging wire to the back.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, use identical frames for joining two frames and either three identical frames or one larger frame in the middle for joining three frames. Lay the frames beside each other to check the effect. Place two frames back to back, mark the hinge placement ensuring it is the same distance from the bottom edges of each frame for secure standing on a table top, and attach two small hinges to the connecting sides of the frames.", "time_sec": 8.01, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.4, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. A lease is a contractual arrangement calling for the lessee to pay the lessor for use of an asset, with common assets including property, buildings, vehicles, and industrial or business equipment.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Leasing is a process by which a firm can obtain the use of a certain fixed asset for which it must pay a series of contractual, periodic, tax deductible payments. The lessee is the receiver of the services or the assets under the lease contract and the lessor is the owner of the assets. A lease is a contractual arrangement calling for the lessee to pay the lessor for use of an asset, with common assets including property, buildings, vehicles, and industrial or business equipment.", "time_sec": 8.893, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.7, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "199", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "gt": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused primarily by bacteria, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci, also known as Streptococcus pyogenes. This is the same bacteria that causes strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria types, such as staphylococcus, are also associated with the disease. The bacteria infect the superficial fascia, a layer of connective tissue below the skin. Prior trauma, such as a cut or scrape, insect bite, burn, or needle puncture wound can serve as a source of infection as well as surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures. In rare cases, fungi can lead to this condition.", "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by bacteria, most commonly group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes), which also cause strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also be associated with the disease. Infections typically occur when bacteria enter the body through minor traumas like cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle punctures, or through surgical incision sites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by bacteria, most commonly group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes), which also cause strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also be associated with the disease. Infections typically occur when bacteria enter the body through minor traumas like cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle punctures, or through surgical incision sites.", "time_sec": 8.458, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 50.91, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "203", "question": "what causes necrotizing fasciitis", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main cause of necrotizing fasciitis is bacterial infection, specifically group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus. Additionally, other types of bacteria have also been associated with the disease. Trauma, such as cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle puncture wounds, can also play a role in the development of necrotizing fasciitis. Surgical incision sites and various surgical procedures can also serve as a source of infection. Therefore, the answer is: Bacterial infection, including group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes) and Staphylococcus, and trauma.", "pred": "Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by bacteria, most commonly group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes), which also cause strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also be associated with the disease. Infections typically occur when bacteria enter the body through minor traumas like cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle punctures, or through surgical incision sites.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Necrotizing fasciitis is caused by bacteria, most commonly group A beta-hemolytic streptococci (Streptococcus pyogenes), which also cause strep throat, impetigo, and rheumatic fever. Other bacteria, such as staphylococcus, can also be associated with the disease. Infections typically occur when bacteria enter the body through minor traumas like cuts, scrapes, insect bites, burns, or needle punctures, or through surgical incision sites.", "time_sec": 8.399, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 45.45, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "204", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard, also known as Swiss chard, is a vegetable with large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a flavor that is stronger and more assertive than spinach, and some people find it bitter. Chard can be eaten raw in salads when it's young, but mature leaves and stalks are usually cooked or sautéed. Chard is actually a type of beet that is grown for its leaves rather than its root. It can produce white, yellow, or red leaf stalks. Chard is highly perishable and should be kept in the refrigerator for only 2 to 3 days.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "time_sec": 8.907, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 48.33, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "205", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked or sautéed. Chard is in the same subspecies as beetroot and is cultivated for leaf production. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when the stems are slightly tougher. Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a minimum amount of time.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "time_sec": 8.869, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 56.14, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "206", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the given passages, Swiss chard (also known as just plain chard) is a type of beet plant that has been selected for its leaf production rather than storage root formation. It produces large, tender deep green leaves with thick, crisp stalks. The leaves have a more assertive and sometimes bitter taste compared to spinach. Swiss chard is a perishable vegetable and should be stored in the refrigerator. It can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "time_sec": 9.1, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.85, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "207", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is what can be inferred about the vegetable \"chard\":\n\n* Chard is a type of beet (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) that has been chosen for leaf production over storage root formation.\n* Chard has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks.\n* The flavor of chard is similar to spinach but with a stronger, more assertive taste (some consider it bitter).\n* Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked to reduce bitterness and bring out a refined flavor.\n* Chard is an attractive ornamental plant that adds color to the vegetable garden.\n* Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator to minimize spoilage.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"What is chard vegetable?\" is: A beet variety (Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima) grown for leaf production, characterized by large, fleshy leaves and stalks with a strong, bitter flavor that becomes more refined with cooking.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "time_sec": 8.888, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 49.69, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "209", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Based on the given passages, chard is a type of vegetable that belongs to the same subspecies as beetroot and is characterized by its large, fleshy leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It has a stronger, more assertive flavor than spinach and can be used raw in salads or cooked like in pizzoccheri. Chard is a beet that has been selected for leaf production rather than storage root formation and can be harvested when young and tender or after maturity. It is an attractive ornamental that adds color to the vegetable garden, but it is extremely perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a maximum of 2-3 days.", "pred": "Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Chard is a beet that has been chosen for leaf production at the expense of storage root formation. It is cultivated for its large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks, which can be used raw in salads when young or cooked when mature. Chard is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor, and it is related to beetroot and other beet cultivars as a descendant of the sea beet, Beta vulgaris subsp. maritima.", "time_sec": 8.966, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 55.93, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "210", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 5.217, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 51.85, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "211", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, with all atoms having the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded, allowing for easy separation of the components using physical methods.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 5.334, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 62.5, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "212", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Here are my answers to the question based on the provided passages:\n\nQ: What are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures?\nA: Based on the passages provided, here are the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures:\n\nElements:\n\n* Are the purest form of a chemical substance (Passage 3)\n* Consist of only one type of atom with the same number of protons (Passage 3)\n\nCompounds:\n\n* Are substances composed of two or more different elements (Passage 3)\n* Are also pure substances (Passage 3)\n\nMixtures:\n\n* Contain two or more substances that are relatively easy to separate (Passage 1)\n* Have a variable composition (Passage 2)\n* Show the properties of their constituent substances (Passage 2)\n* Can be separated by physical means (Passage 2)", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 5.347, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 37.93, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "213", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are:\n\n* Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom. They have a fixed composition and cannot be broken down into simpler substances by physical means.\n* Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements that are chemically bonded together. They have a fixed composition and are pure substances.\n* Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and retain their own identity. They have a variable composition and can be separated by physical means.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures are their composition, bonding, and separability. Elements are homogeneous and have a fixed composition, compounds are heterogeneous and have a fixed composition, and mixtures are heterogeneous and have a variable composition. Additionally, elements and compounds are chemically bonded, while mixtures are not.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: Elements are pure substances composed of only one type of atom. Compounds are pure substances made of two or more different elements chemically bonded together. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the components are not chemically bonded and can be separated by physical means.", "time_sec": 5.247, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 43.97, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.", "time_sec": 13.774, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 75.39, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "215", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To wash wine glasses properly, start by using hot water and mild detergent to clean the outside of the glass. If there are stubborn wine residues, use baking soda to dissolve them by mixing a small amount of soda with hot water and letting it sit in the glass for a few minutes. For cleaning the inside of the glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. Rinse thoroughly with hot water and dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth. To avoid damage, wash one wine glass at a time, use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed, and cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.", "time_sec": 13.66, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 70.51, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To wash wine glasses properly, first lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one glass at a time to avoid damage, using a small amount of mild detergent only where needed—specifically in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand to protect the stem. For stubborn wine residue, dissolve a small amount of baking soda in hot water, let it stand in the glass for a few minutes, and then rinse thoroughly. After rinsing, dry the glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel. Use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles to clean the inside of the glass, and ensure the glasses are dried completely to prevent red wine stains, especially if left overnight.", "time_sec": 13.838, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 59.65, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "221", "question": "how to peel potatoes fast", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to peel potatoes fast:\n\n1. Score the potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n2. Boil the potatoes for about 15 minutes.\n3. Place the potatoes in a bowl of ice water and swish them around for a few seconds.\n4. Remove the potatoes from the water and remove the skin.\n\nAlternatively, you can also try the following method:\n\n1. Cut the potato skin, making a cut all around the potato lengthwise.\n2. Boil the potato in a pot of boiling water.\n3. Plunge the potato in ice water for 10 seconds.\n4. Rub the potato with both hands, and the skin should fall right off.\n\nThese methods should help you peel potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "pred": "To peel potatoes fast, first cut the potato skin lengthwise all around the potato, being careful to slice only the skin and not the potato itself. Then, boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. After boiling, plunge the potato into ice water for 10 seconds to cool it down and cause the skin to shrink. Finally, remove the potato from the water and rub it with both hands to easily remove the skin. This method is mentioned in passage 3 and passage 2, which both describe steps to peel cooked potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To peel potatoes fast, first cut the potato skin lengthwise all around the potato, being careful to slice only the skin and not the potato itself. Then, boil the potato in a pot of water for about 15 minutes. After boiling, plunge the potato into ice water for 10 seconds to cool it down and cause the skin to shrink. Finally, remove the potato from the water and rub it with both hands to easily remove the skin. This method is mentioned in passage 3 and passage 2, which both describe steps to peel cooked potatoes quickly and efficiently.", "time_sec": 9.975, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 52.7, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "time_sec": 11.675, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.45, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "224", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "To fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Turn off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms.\n3. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n4. Fill the tank by turning on the water valve and then flushing the toilet. Adjust the lift chain as needed by moving the metal clip up or down a few links. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n5. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm. Make sure it is securely fastened.\n6. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If it flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "time_sec": 11.502, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 67.46, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "225", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet before starting the repair (Passage 1).\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms, and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm (Passage 1).\n3. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to check for correct operation. If necessary, readjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links (Passage 2).\n4. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm (Passage 3). Secure it using pliers to ensure it is tightly fastened.\n5. Turn the water valve back on and test the toilet's flush function. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm (Passage 3).\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide instructions on how to fix a specific issue with the lift valve, such as a stuck or leaking valve.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "time_sec": 11.607, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 60.61, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "226", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fix a lift valve in a toilet:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve and any remaining pieces of the broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install the new flapper valve and connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, making sure it is securely fastened.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank and flush the toilet to test for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the chain as needed to ensure a proper flush. Cut off any excess chain to prevent tangling.\n\nNote: If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_nemotron", "raw_output": "Answer: To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "time_sec": 11.528, "has_vcd": false, "degraded_reason": "text-only: no visual to distort", "nemotron": {"runtime": "transformers-5.6.2-trust-remote-code", "enable_thinking": false, "alpha": 0.1, "noise_std": 0.1}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 61.04, "GAVIE-Rel": -1.0, "GAVIE-Acc": -1.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "227", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Here's a brief answer on how to fix a lift valve in a toilet based on the given passages:\n\nTo fix a lift valve in a toilet, follow these steps:\n\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms. Remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain for a 1.6 gallon per flush toilet.\n4. Open the water valve to fill the tank. Flush the toilet to check for correct operation.\n5. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links if necessary. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent it from getting tangled.\n6. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle. If a screw is included, screw it in tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge of the lift arm. Use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened.\n8. Turn the water valve back on and test out the flush of the toilet. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "To fix the lift valve in a toilet, first shut off the water supply valve. Then, remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove any remaining broken lift chain from the lift arm. Push the small solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle, and if a screw is included, screw it in tightly until secure. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm, which is the hole closest to the edge, and use pliers to ensure it is securely fastened. Turn the water valve back on and test the flush. If the toilet flushes slowly, adjust the chain to make it a little tighter on the lift arm.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_vcd_